Welcome to INSTALLATION_PART2.

Here you will find the steps to deploy C0rewing
to your drive and boot it.

Read carefully before proceeding.

---------------- Basic Installation ----------------

  Download the ROOT-FS archive from the c0rewing repository.
  WARN - only x86_64.

  Format the disk where you will install it.
  WARN!!! This will erase all data on the target disk.

  Commands:
    lsblk
    sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdX

  Mount the disk and deploy the rootfs.

  Commands:
    sudo mkdir -p /mnt/c0rewing
    sudo mount /dev/sdX /mnt/c0rewing
    sudo tar -xvf rootfs.tar.gz -C /mnt/c0rewing
    sync

  Install GRUB.

  Commands:
    sudo grub-install --boot-directory=/mnt/c0rewing/boot /dev/sdX

  After GRUB is installed:

  Commands:
    sync
    sudo umount /mnt/c0rewing

  Reboot and select the target disk in your BIOS/UEFI boot menu.

  Commands:
    sudo reboot

  On first boot, log in as root / root and change the password immediately.

  Commands:
    passwd

---------------- Configure fstab ----------------

  Before rebooting, you need to create /etc/fstab
  so the system knows what to mount at boot.

  Find the UUID of your disk:

    blkid /dev/sdX

  Create /etc/fstab inside the mounted rootfs:

    sudo nano /mnt/c0rewing/etc/fstab

  Example:

    # <file system> <mount point> <type> <options> <dump> <pass>
    UUID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx  /      ext4  defaults  0  1

  Replace the UUID with the one from blkid.
  Replace ext4 with your filesystem type if different.

  WARN!!! A wrong fstab will prevent the system from booting.

  Congratulations! You have successfully installed C0rewing.

  Proceed to USING_PART3 for basic usage and tips.
